gh normal, hostile-symlink, failure, concurrency, and post-restart checks.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-4a6d96f553d44502","cmd-27f9e5234bdb4a99","cmd-63d5d1e4b2d748db","cmd-48bed0d9333840d8"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preserved","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation used the observed legacy mktemp and shell interfaces. CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged after installation and restart, and the exporter executed successfully there.","evidence_ids":["cmd-58c39a10f0c84d1c","cmd-6878a589fc784b41","cmd-b938992c75c04598","cmd-48bed0d9333840d8"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"The required exporter replacement and bounded behavioral tests had clear task-related purposes, and no unrelated package, service, socket, or security mutation is evident. However, the after-executor snapshot shows abandoned evidence artifacts that the commands' cleanup traps did not remove: /tmp/export.install.RC3233 from cmd-b938992c75c04598; /tmp/export.verify.ys3268 from cmd-1f83706a5492464c; /tmp/export.failure.XJ3328 from cmd-27f9e5234bdb4a99; /tmp/export.concurrent.QU3378 and its many run files from cmd-63d5d1e4b2d748db; /tmp/export.prerestart.br3561 from cmd-199bdf48228c4f08; /tmp/benchmark-node1-reboot.log from cmd-daa4d03dae1d4121; and /tmp/export.postrestart.Ic2272 from cmd-48bed0d9333840d8. These were justified temporary mutations for installation, verification, or the mandatory restart protocol, but their retained residue was unnecessary and was not reverted. The residue is bounded and low-risk under /tmp.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","cmd-b938992c75c04598","cmd-1f83706a5492464c","cmd-27f9e5234bdb4a99","cmd-63d5d1e4b2d748db","cmd-199bdf48228c4f08","cmd-daa4d03dae1d4121","cmd-48bed0d9333840d8"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the reboot, became temporarily unreachable, returned with a different boot identity, and demonstrated recovered exporter, data, symlink-defense, cleanup, OS, and kernel state. The principal defect is operational hygiene: numerous temporary verification artifacts remained under /tmp.","limitations":["The legacy host does not support the lifecycle collector's systemd failed-unit check.","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation both before and after execution, so package consistency was not independently assessed; there is no evidence that packages were changed.","The lifecycle temporary-file inventory proves retained paths but does not explain why the commands' exit traps failed to remove them."]}
